{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>The city which they had defiled.</b> For had such a thing not already been abhorrent to them, Shechem would not have done so. Indeed, this was a practice customary among them — that the leaders of the city took the daughters of the people without authority, as wives or as concubines, after the manner of וַיִּקְחוּ לָהֶם נָשִׁים מִכֹּל אֲשֶׁר בָּחָרוּ (Genesis 6:2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:18.170299365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}